    <textArea id="c-dependencies-title" x="1656" y="744" width="1432" height="40" fill="#1a1a1a" font-family="noto_sans" font-size="22" text-align="left" font-weight="bold">Inputs and coordination</textArea>
    <textArea id="c-controls-title" x="64" y="1120" width="1432" height="40" fill="#1a1a1a" font-family="noto_sans" font-size="22" text-align="left" font-weight="bold">Operating controls to agree</textArea>
    <textArea id="c-decisions-title" x="1656" y="1120" width="1432" height="40" fill="#1a1a1a" font-family="noto_sans" font-size="22" text-align="left" font-weight="bold">Open decisions for review</textArea>
    <rect id="c-proof" x="64" y="824" width="1432" height="224" data-content="• Baseline works; elevated operations are denied before activation.&lt;br&gt;• Ineligible, pending and declined requests do not gain privilege.&lt;br&gt;• Active grants permit only the agreed target operation/scope.&lt;br&gt;• Expiry/revocation removes elevation; valid baseline remains.&lt;br&gt;• Delays, remaining access, audit and failed-removal escalation are tested." fill="#ddddd8" stroke="#a8a8a0" stroke-width="2" data-text-color="#434339" data-font-family="noto_sans" data-font-size="22" data-text-align="left" data-text-align-vertical="middle" />
    <rect id="c-dependencies" x="1656" y="824" width="1432" height="224" data-content="• Agreed team/job baseline and identity mappings from 08/09.&lt;br&gt;• Target roles, resource/repository scope and effective-access inventory.&lt;br&gt;• Supported elevation service, licensing/integration and owners.&lt;br&gt;• Requester/approver test identities and an approved pilot scope.&lt;br&gt;• Audit/alerts from 07 and owned catalog/runbooks through 06." fill="#ddddd8" stroke="#a8a8a0" stroke-width="2" data-text-color="#434339" data-font-family="noto_sans" data-font-size="22" data-text-align="left" data-text-align-vertical="middle" />
    <rect id="c-controls" x="64" y="1200" width="1432" height="224" data-content="• Explicit administrators, eligible requesters, approvers and owners.&lt;br&gt;• Reviewed role/scope changes, justification and bounded duration.&lt;br&gt;• Verified activation/removal, audit trail and exception ownership.&lt;br&gt;• Emergency/recovery access and overdue-removal response.&lt;br&gt;• Recurring eligibility, overlapping-grant and standing-access review." fill="#ffe86d" stroke="#cbb333" stroke-width="2" data-text-color="#574900" data-font-family="noto_sans" data-font-size="22" data-text-align="left" data-text-align-vertical="middle" />
    <rect id="c-decisions" x="1656" y="1200" width="1432" height="224" data-content="• Which baseline/elevated tasks, roles and target scopes come first?&lt;br&gt;• Google Cloud PAM scope; any separately supported GitHub mechanism?&lt;br&gt;• Who is eligible, who approves, and what duration/reason is required?&lt;br&gt;• How are early ending, propagation/sessions and emergencies handled?&lt;br&gt;• Who owns removal failures, audit retention and recurring review?" fill="#ffe86d" stroke="#cbb333" stroke-width="2" data-text-color="#574900" data-font-family="noto_sans" data-font-size="22" data-text-align="left" data-text-align-vertical="middle" />
    <rect id="c-boundaries" x="64" y="1504" width="3024" height="160" data-content="&lt;b&gt;Elevation grants access; the task still follows its normal change and execution controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Use &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/pam-request-temporary-elevated-access&quot;&gt;Google PAM grant lifecycle guidance&lt;/a&gt; for the chosen cloud implementation. Prove target activation/removal; group-based downstream access must meet the required timing and scope.&lt;br&gt;Coordinate 08/09 identity decisions, 01 execution controls and 06/07 documentation/audit operations. Exact roles, target mechanisms, duration, approvals and rollout sequence remain decisions." fill="#ddddd8" stroke="#a8a8a0" stroke-width="2" data-text-color="#434339" data-font-family="noto_sans" data-font-size="22" data-text-align="left" data-text-align-vertical="middle" />
